    "Although the reaction is strongly exothermic, a bottle of 3% hydrogen peroxide lasts for months, because the activation energy is high. Iodide ion speeds up the reaction, and the enzyme catalase, found in nearly all aerobic cells, speeds it up enormously. Figure 1 compares the energy profiles with and without catalase.",
