    "Normally, electron transport and ATP synthesis are coupled: electrons flow only as fast as protons can return through ATP synthase. Researchers studied isolated mitochondria supplied with malate, an NADH-linked substrate, plus ADP and phosphate. They measured O<sub>2</sub> consumption and ATP synthesis with several inhibitors (Table 1; values relative to control; hypothetical data).",
